    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nAn exceptional opportunity to acquire a superb five-bedroom detached family home, ideally positioned on a private site within The Chantries, one of Balbriggan's most prestigious and mature residential developments. Beautifully maintained and superbly presented throughout, No. 14 combines generous proportions, versatile accommodation and a wonderful sense of privacy, making it an ideal home for modern family living.\nThe property is particularly impressive from the outset, with its handsome double-fronted façade and full red-brick exterior creating an attractive and timeless first impression. To the side, a large driveway provides excellent off-street parking together with valuable vehicular access to the rear, while the private site offers a wonderful setting for family life.\nInternally, the accommodation is both spacious and versatile, with two large reception rooms providing excellent living and entertaining space, complemented by a separate kitchen and dining room. The generous layout offers plentiful accommodation and can be easily configured to suit the changing needs of any family, whether requiring dedicated bedrooms, home office space, play areas or additional reception rooms.\nUpstairs, the principal bedroom is particularly impressive in scale and benefits from its own ensuite, while the remaining bedrooms are generously proportioned and complemented by well-appointed family accommodation. The overall presentation is of a home that has been lovingly cared for and maintained, allowing the new owners to move in and enjoy immediately.\nThe Chantries enjoys an enviable location adjacent to Balbriggan Golf Club, surrounded by established residential surroundings and mature landscaping. The development is highly regarded for its attractive setting and convenient access to the town and surrounding amenities. Commuters are particularly well catered for, with Exit 5 of the M1 just minutes away by car, providing easy access to Dublin Airport, the M50 and Dublin City.\nHeating is provided by oil-fired central heating, while the property also benefits from double-glazed hardwood windows.\nOverall, No. 14 The Chantries represents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial and wonderfully presented detached family home in one of Balbriggan's most sought-after residential locations. Combining impressive proportions, excellent versatility, private outdoor space and superb commuter connectivity, this is a home that is sure to appeal to discerning purchasers seeking quality family accommodation in an established and highly regarded setting."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPorch area - 1.76m x 1.76m\nwith tiled flooring and internal glass doors.\n\nEntrance Hall - 3.3m x 5.05m\nwith tiled flooring and guest wc\n\nSitting / family room - 3.17m x 4.77m\nwith tiled flooring, dual aspect with excellent natural light, situated the front of the property\n\nLiving Room - 3.17m x 5.58m\nwith carpet flooring, open fire with hearth and backing, double door access to dining room\n\nDining room - 3.24m x 3.5m\nwith carpet flooring, sliding door access to rear and door to kitchen area\n\nKitchen - 3.5m x 6.1m\nwith tiled flooring, fitted kitchen with worktops, eating area and open fire with backboiler and tiled backing and hearth, door to utility room\n\nUtility Room - 1.67m x 1.98m\nwith tileed flooring, plumbed for washing machine and door to rear.\n\nLanding area - \nwith window\n\nBedrom One - 4.98m x 3.5m\nwith extensive built in wardrobes, large double bedroom with ensuite shower room which has been upgraded in recent times.\n\nBedroom Two - 4.22m x 3.46m\nDouble bedroom with built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom Three - 2.73m x 3.46m\ndouble bedroom\n\nBedroom Four - 3.76m x 3.5m\ndouble bedroom with built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom Five - 2.15m x 3.46\nlarge single bedroom\n\nFamily Bathroom - 2.57m x 2.02m\nwith tilde flooring and walls, bath with shower above, wc and whb, with attic access and hot press\n\n"
      },
      {
